@* Exercise 028 — AuthorizeViewAndAuthState (reference solution).
   Goal:   Gate two sections of a page by authorization state: one visible to
           any authenticated user, one visible only to the "manager" role.
           Implement ResolveManagerRole so the manager AuthorizeView requires
           the right role name.
   Drills: AuthenticationStateProvider, AuthorizeView, cascading auth state.
   Passes: attack facts - an anonymous state renders neither the manager nor
                          the authenticated section; a state authenticated
                          without the manager role renders the authenticated
                          section but not the manager section;
           use facts     - a manager-role state renders both sections, and the
                          anonymous state renders the NotAuthorized content, so
                          the page is not simply blank. *@

<AuthorizeView Roles="@ResolveManagerRole()">
    <Authorized>
        <div id="manager-section">Manager tools.</div>
    </Authorized>
</AuthorizeView>

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <div id="authenticated-section">Member area.</div>
    </Authorized>
    <NotAuthorized>
        <div id="anonymous-section">Please sign in to continue.</div>
    </NotAuthorized>
</AuthorizeView>

@code {
    private static string ResolveManagerRole() => "manager";
}
